# ignore any IDEA project files anywhere
**/.idea/
# IntelliJ sandbox directories
**/idea-sandbox/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/settings.local.json

# Terraform (local runs only — CI uses ephemeral runners and a remote backend,
# but local bootstrap runs like sharing-server/infra/bootstrap leave these
# behind; state files can contain plaintext secrets, never commit them)
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Graphify output. manifest.json + cache/ ARE committed so a fresh clone or cloud
# agent can run `graphify --update` from a warm cache instead of a full rescan.
# Everything else (graph.json/html, GRAPH_REPORT.md, cost.json) is regenerable, and
# .graphify_python/.graphify_root are absolute machine-specific paths — never commit those.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/manifest.json
!graphify-out/cache/
!graphify-out/cache/**

# Stray/misplaced graphify cache (wrong working directory on a past run)
src/graphify-out/
